# Known Issues

The file `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` at the project root tracks known bugs, limitations, and
deferred work items.

## How to Use

- **Before working on a component**: Check `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` for known problems
  that may affect your work or that your work could address.
- **When discovering a new issue**: Add an entry with status, date, component,
  problem description, and any known root cause or workaround.
- **When resolving an issue**: Update the status to "Resolved" with the date and
  a brief note on the fix, but keep the entry for historical context.

## Current Open Issues

- **ML Table Detection underperforms heuristic** -- `MLTableDetection/TableDetectorML.py`
  exists and has been trained through four iterations (v2, v4, v5, v5b). The best model
  (v4) achieves mAP@0.5 of 0.66 on `generic3.pdf` but still trails the heuristic
  `PanelSearchToolV25` which finds all 6 panels. Adding negative examples (v5, v5b)
  caused regressions. v4 remains the best Table Transformer model. The training skill
  recommends escalating to RF-DETR (Apache 2.0) if further improvement is needed.

- **ML Page Classifier created** -- `PageFilter/PageClassifierML.py` provides a
  MobileNetV2 binary classifier for page-level "has panel / no panel" decisions.
  Trained on 35 images (28 pos, 7 neg), achieves 100% val accuracy. Designed as
  a faster drop-in replacement for PageFilterV4 (~250 ms/page vs ~1-3s). Not yet
  integrated into `uplink_server.py` (still imports `PageFilterV3`).

- **uplink_server.py imports PageFilterV3** -- The latest heuristic is V4, and
  the ML classifier is available, but `uplink_server.py` still imports
  `PageFilter.PageFilterV3`. See `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` for details.
